{ Fool's Mate is generally regarded as something that should never happen in play, unless the opponent wanted to end the game without resigning. It does serve to interest those fascinated by short mates, however, and signifies the importance of the king bishop pawn. }
1. f3 (1. f4 { Alternatively it could start with f4. } 1... e5 2. g4 Qh4#) (1. g4 { This is called A00, Grob Opening and might be a more common opening. } 1... e5 2. f3 (2. f4 Qh4#) 2... Qh4# (2... c5 3. Kf2)) 1... e5 2. g4 Qh4# { Surprisingly, there are games even within lichess of players opening this way and not spotting the mate. } *


