[UTCDate "2016.06.01"]
[UTCTime "16:34:42"]

1. e4 e5 { Starts with C20, King Pawn Game } 2. Qh5 g6 { Black attempts to threaten the queen but has ignored his unprotected king pawn. } (2... Nc6 { If instead black notices his pawn's danger... } { [%cal Yc6e5] } 3. Bc4 { White threaten's mate by queen on f7. } { [%cal Rh5f7,Rc4f7] } 3... Nf6 (3... g6 { Black can play g-pawn as before now because the king pawn is protected. } 4. Qf3 { White can now retreat the queen and continue threatening mate by queen on f7. } { [%cal Rc4f7,Rf3f7] } 4... Bg7 (4... Nf6 { Here, black has finally rebuffed white from landing Scholar's Mate. }) 5. Qxf7#) 4. Qxf7#) 3. Qxe5+ { Black has three choices to get out of check: queen, bishop, knight. } { [%cal Gg8e7,Gf8e7,Gd8e7] } 3... Qe7 4. Qxh8 { Any choice, white gets the rook. } *


